  "notes": "PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: the prompt says throughput results are taken \"at a specific data size\", but the ground-truth filter patterns do not test any data size (only its logical IDs mention 52MB), so that clause has no check. Language detection is by FilterPattern regex (the filter must select that language's events to publish a language-specific metric). Namespace and metric names are not stated, so only five distinct namespaces are required; binding each namespace to one language is not expressible (no inequality join). filters_on_group passes if some filter targets the log group (ref/join have no 'all' quantifier). Retention and outputs are detail per the rubric. Scored on 5 real candidates: all pass every core check."
